📊 The Data Analysis Process | From Raw Data to Insights

Data analysis is not just about working with numbers. It is a structured process of transforming raw data into meaningful insights that can support better business decisions.

🔹 1. Define the Problem
Understand the business question, objective, and what you need to discover from the data.

🔹 2. Collect Data
Gather relevant data from sources such as databases, Excel files, APIs, surveys, websites, and business systems.

🔹 3. Clean & Prepare Data
Handle missing values, duplicates, incorrect formats, outliers, and inconsistencies to make the data reliable.

🔹 4. Explore the Data
Identify patterns, trends, relationships, and unusual observations using statistics and visualizations.

🔹 5. Analyze the Data
Apply formulas, SQL queries, statistical methods, and analytical techniques to answer the business questions.

🔹 6. Visualize the Insights
Use charts, dashboards, and reports to present findings in a clear and understandable way.

🔹 7. Communicate Results
Explain what the data tells us, why it matters, and what actions can be taken based on the findings.

🔹 8. Make Data-Driven Decisions
Turn insights into practical recommendations that help improve business performance.

🚀 The complete journey:
Problem → Collect → Clean → Explore → Analyze → Visualize → Communicate → Decide

A good data analyst doesn't just find numbers — they turn data into actionable insights.
